  "content": {
    "id": "p21-p2-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "2",
    "prompt": "Solve the following for $\\theta\\in[0,360^\\circ]$.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p21-p2-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$\\cos^2\\theta=\\sin\\theta-1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\theta=90^\\circ$.",
          "worked": "Use $\\cos^2\\theta=1-\\sin^2\\theta$.\n$$\\begin{align*}1-\\sin^2\\theta&=\\sin\\theta-1\\\\\\sin^2\\theta+\\sin\\theta-2&=0\\\\(\\sin\\theta+2)(\\sin\\theta-1)&=0\\\\\\sin\\theta&=-2\\text{ or }1\\end{align*}$$\nReject $\\sin\\theta=-2$, since $-1\\leq\\sin\\theta\\leq1$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\sin\\theta&=1\\\\\\theta&=90^\\circ\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 40
      },
      {
        "id": "p21-p2-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$\\sec^2\\theta-\\tan\\theta-1=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\theta=0^\\circ,45^\\circ,180^\\circ,225^\\circ,360^\\circ$.",
          "worked": "Use $\\sec^2\\theta=1+\\tan^2\\theta$.\n$$\\begin{align*}1+\\tan^2\\theta-\\tan\\theta-1&=0\\\\\\tan^2\\theta-\\tan\\theta&=0\\\\\\tan\\theta(\\tan\\theta-1)&=0\\\\\\tan\\theta&=0\\text{ or }1\\end{align*}$$\nFor $\\tan\\theta=0$, $\\theta=0^\\circ,180^\\circ,360^\\circ$. For $\\tan\\theta=1$, $\\theta=45^\\circ,225^\\circ$. All these angles have $\\cos\\theta\\ne0$, so the original equation is defined.\nThus $\\theta=0^\\circ,45^\\circ,180^\\circ,225^\\circ,360^\\circ$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 39
      },
      {
        "id": "p21-p2-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$\\cos^2\\theta-\\sin^2\\theta+3\\cos\\theta+2=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\theta=120^\\circ,180^\\circ,240^\\circ$.",
          "worked": "Use $\\sin^2\\theta=1-\\cos^2\\theta$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\cos^2\\theta-(1-\\cos^2\\theta)\\qquad&\\\\{}+3\\cos\\theta+2&=0\\\\2\\cos^2\\theta+3\\cos\\theta+1&=0\\\\(2\\cos\\theta+1)(\\cos\\theta+1)&=0\\\\\\cos\\theta&=-\\frac12\\text{ or }-1\\end{align*}$$\nFor $\\cos\\theta=-\\frac12$, $\\theta=120^\\circ,240^\\circ$. For $\\cos\\theta=-1$, $\\theta=180^\\circ$.\nThus $\\theta=120^\\circ,180^\\circ,240^\\circ$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 45
      },
      {
        "id": "p21-p2-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$\\tan^2\\theta-\\sec\\theta-1=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\theta=60^\\circ,180^\\circ,300^\\circ$.",
          "worked": "Use $\\tan^2\\theta=\\sec^2\\theta-1$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\sec^2\\theta-1-\\sec\\theta-1&=0\\\\\\sec^2\\theta-\\sec\\theta-2&=0\\\\(\\sec\\theta-2)(\\sec\\theta+1)&=0\\\\\\sec\\theta&=2\\text{ or }-1\\\\\\cos\\theta&=\\frac12\\text{ or }-1\\end{align*}$$\nFor $\\cos\\theta=\\frac12$, $\\theta=60^\\circ,300^\\circ$. For $\\cos\\theta=-1$, $\\theta=180^\\circ$. The original equation is defined at all three angles.\nThus $\\theta=60^\\circ,180^\\circ,300^\\circ$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 43
      }
    ]
  },
